1. What you may do

   a. Read and study the source code.

   b. Run the Software as published, for yourself or for your organization, including installing
      it on your own server ("self-hosting") for a kurin, a stanytsia or another Plast unit. You may
      use the official release bundles or build the Software from this repository without changes.

   c. Configure the Software through its documented settings (environment variables, `.env` files,
      configuration files and the setup wizard). Configuration is not modification, as long as the
      conditions in section 2 are kept.

   d. Contribute. You may fork this repository and change your copy solely in order to propose
      those changes back to this repository as an issue or a pull request. A fork made for that
      purpose must not be deployed, published, distributed or used for anything else. Larger ideas
      should be discussed with the Author in an issue before any work starts.

